---
globs:
  - "src/agentWork/**"
  - "src/review/publish/**"
  - "src/review/placement/reviewInlinePublish.ts"
  - "src/github/prSurfaceMutation.ts"
  - "src/github/recoverPrSurfaceMutation.ts"
  - "src/agent/*/publish*.ts"
  - "src/agent/*/submit*Tool.ts"
---

Every PR-surface GitHub mutation runs inside `withOperationIntent` (`src/agentWork/withOperationIntent.ts`) with a key builder from the same module (`reviewInlineBatchOperationKey`, `reviewSummaryOperationKey`, `askReplyOperationKey`, `descriptionPrBodyOperationKey`, `triagePushOperationKey`). The intent row is persisted before the call and reconciled into `publish_records`, which stay authoritative for what was posted. Status `failed` is provider-proven non-acceptance and may retry; `outcome_unknown` is never auto-remutated and resolves only from a publish record or exact remote evidence (`recoverPrSurfaceMutation.ts`), else it fails closed. Void and `T | undefined` callers set `allowsUndefinedResult`; a typed `recover` that cannot rebuild `T` stays `outcome_unknown`. Leased work passes `leaseEpoch`, and the frame calls `assertPrActorLeaseHeld` immediately before the call and again before completion (ADR 0030). Do not call a mutation outside this frame or wrap it in a retry loop.
